Step 0 is now decisive: Section II’s “LIMSAT” object is a 0–1 literal-selection vector constrained by a variable-incidence block and a clause-incidence block. Feasibility is exactly SAT feasibility; the construction itself is polynomial, but solving remains a SAT/0–1 ILP search. The paper also explicitly reports Gurobi as the mechanical solver and runtimes from seconds to thousands of seconds, so a Track A claim based only on worst-case NP-completeness would be dishonest. I’m evaluating a Track B construction that keeps the paper’s LIMSAT matrix native and hides a compact algebraic structure inside the clauses.
