codex
Implemented the verified Track B generator based on the paper’s Section II.B LIMSAT construction ([arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1803.09963)).

Created:

- [gen_1803_09963.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.09963/gen_1803_09963.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.09963/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.09963/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.09963/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [.meta.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.09963/.meta.json)

Local gates G1–G9(c) pass. Highlights:

- 0/200,000 random guesses succeeded.
- Four attacks failed across 8/8 seeds each.
- The polynomial reference algorithm solved 8/8, honestly reported for Track B.
- Mechanical cost: mean 673,978 scalar operations.
- Compact route: 224 XORs.
- Answer: 112 elements, 336 characters.
- Canonical-key tests: 60/60 invariance checks and 20/20 distinct instances.

The only blocker is external: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “key limit exceeded” on every call. Therefore no valid four-vendor hardness verdict or G9 hinted/placebo transcripts could be produced. The failed calls are preserved as API errors and were not counted as oracle failures. A funded `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is required to resume Step 4.
